    description: "go.py still emits call destinations with the retired \":unresolved\" kind slot at four sites (go.py ~4843, 4933, 5026, 5071: f\"go:external:0-0:{callee_name}:unresolved\" and f\"go:{_slot}:0-0:{callee_name}:unresolved\"), and boundary synthesis does not mint a node for that slot since ADR-0036 ruling 2 made external_symbol the kind. Result: dangling edges in the default output. Measured 2026-11-03 on caddy (curriculum_repos/caddy, dev cd6aeed541, identical with and without the INV-saruf fix; lab ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/saruf_11032026/caddy_dangling.txt): 7 calls edges whose dst is go:external:0-0:{RemoteAddr,LocalAddr,GetRecords,SetRecords}:unresolved, from modules/caddytls (interface-method calls through net.Conn / libdns), with no such node in the output. test_phase_de_reorder's G2 asserts zero dangling edges for its fixture; on a Go corpus repo the invariant does not hold. Fix shape: route these four arms through make_unresolved_edge (F-unresolved-edge-bypass / INV-hazov rule 3 sees helper-built edges), which gives the external_symbol slot; measure the dangling count on caddy and cert-manager to 0. Check first whether WI-jolif or another item already owns these sites."  # 681d
